/* book Worked example 2: Q: Find the area enclosed by the adjusted traverse of the closing-error chapter: A (1000.00, 1000.00), B (1141.45, 1141.48), C (1268.76, 1014.25) and D (1188.78, 875.74), eastings and northings in metres.
   1. A: 1000.00 × (1141.48 − 875.74) = 1000.00 × 265.74 = 265 740.0
   2. B: 1141.45 × (1014.25 − 1000.00) = 1141.45 × 14.25 = 16 265.7
   3. C: 1268.76 × (875.74 − 1141.48) = 1268.76 × (−265.74) = −337 160.3
   4. D: 1188.78 × (1000.00 − 1014.25) = 1188.78 × (−14.25) = −16 940.1
   5. Sum = 265 740.0 + 16 265.7 − 337 160.3 − 16 940.1 = −72 094.7 m². The sign is negative because A, B, C, D run clockwise.
   6. Area = 72 094.7/2 = 36 047 m² = 3.605 ha.
   Answer: The traverse encloses 36 047 m², about 3.60 ha; the negative raw sum only shows that the corners were taken clockwise. */
